## LWJGL's native-library extraction cache, created at runtime when running the client
## (wherever the working directory happened to be when it was run):
.lwjgl/

## Runtime-generated local data (design.md 3.7/3.8) - a game's per-player snapshots/action
## journals, its game-meta file, and a real account store (login/salted password hash) could
## land in any directory a server happens to be launched from, not just server/target. None
## of this has a fixed name/path yet since the actual persistence code doesn't exist yet -
## broaden this once it does (matching the sibling projects' data/accounts.json pattern).
data/

## Client-local settings (design.md 3.8 - volume, resolution, keybindings, etc., never
## server/account state): no fixed filename decided yet - broaden once it exists.
client-settings.json
